(function(root){
'use strict';
const C=root.PreparationCore,$=id=>document.getElementById(id),section=document.createElement('section');section.className='card';section.id='preparation';section.style.marginTop='32px';
section.innerHTML=`<div class="eyebrow">Preparation &amp; chance</div><h2 style="margin-top:16px">How much planning is worth it?</h2><p>A bad result does not prove you failed to prepare. Compare a lighter plan with more preparation, including research, practice, checks and recovery. Preparation can change the odds; it cannot remove uncertainty.</p><p class="helper">Compare ways of preparing for the same goal. This additional score does not replace the main decision’s limits or tell you whether to pursue the goal itself.</p><p><a href="#preparationResearch">Read the evidence and equations ↓</a></p><form id="prepForm"><label for="prepContext">Decision type</label><select id="prepContext"><option value="everyday">Class / tasks / rest</option><option value="purchase">Buying something</option><option value="relationship">Time with someone</option><option value="income">Work / income</option></select><label for="prepTask">What are you deciding?</label><input id="prepTask" maxlength="160" required placeholder="How much should I prepare for this class?"><label for="prepDefinition">One observable success, and the deadline for checking it</label><input id="prepDefinition" maxlength="160" required placeholder="Finish the class exercise by Friday"><p class="helper">Use the same definition for both plans. This two-outcome model groups all other results together; use separate scenarios if important outcomes differ. Ratings are personal value, not measured happiness.</p><div class="row"><div><label for="prepSuccess">Value if success happens · 0–100</label><input id="prepSuccess" type="number" min="0" max="100" required></div><div><label for="prepFailure">Value of the other outcome · 0–100</label><input id="prepFailure" type="number" min="0" max="100" required></div></div><div id="prepPlans" class="row"></div><details><summary>What matters to you, and hard limits</summary><p>Starting weights are editable defaults, not inferred preferences. These priorities apply to this preparation comparison. Each cost is the total additional planning cost for that plan, including recovery. Do not add benefits already in the outcome values. Scores are not comparable with a differently configured decision.</p><div id="prepPriorities"></div><label for="prepDeclined"><input type="checkbox" id="prepDeclined" style="width:auto"> This would go against someone’s refusal or request for space</label><p class="helper">For relationships, success must respect the other person’s choice. Spending or preparation never creates an entitlement to affection.</p></details><label for="prepBasis">What supports your probability estimates?</label><textarea id="prepBasis" maxlength="2000" required placeholder="Comparable past attempts, an external base rate, or clearly marked guess"></textarea><label for="prepIfThen">A small prevention or backup plan · optional</label><input id="prepIfThen" maxlength="300" placeholder="If the bus is late, I’ll join the online class"><button class="primary" type="submit">Compare preparation with chance</button><button class="quiet" id="prepExample" type="button">Try a labeled example</button></form><div id="prepResult" role="status" aria-live="polite"></div><button class="quiet" id="prepSave" type="button" disabled>Save preparation forecast</button><p id="prepSaveStatus" role="status"></p><h3>Check your forecasts against experience</h3><p>After saving, open the decision in Your reflections and record the chosen plan, actual planning time and whether the defined outcome happened. Only the chosen plan is observed.</p><div id="prepEvidence" class="math-table"></div><details id="preparationResearch"><summary>Research, equations and limits · reviewed November 4, 2026</summary><p><b>Specific plans can help.</b> Gollwitzer &amp; Sheeran’s 2006 meta-analysis of 94 independent tests found an average standardized effect d = 0.65 on goal attainment for implementation intentions: specifying when, where and how to act. This is not a 65% success boost, and cannot be converted into your probability. <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/S0065-2601(06)38002-1" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Original meta-analysis</a>.</p><p><b>Effort is only part of the picture.</b> Macnamara and colleagues’ 2014 meta-analysis found deliberate practice associated with different amounts of performance variation across domains: 26% in games, 21% in music, 18% in sports, 4% in education and under 1% in professions. These between-person associations concern structured practice, not all preparation, and do not identify causal effects. Unexplained variation includes ability, opportunity, measurement and circumstances; it is not a measured “luck percentage.” <a href="https://doi.org/10.1177/0956797614535810" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Original meta-analysis and correction link</a>.</p><p><b>Expected utility:</b> EU(plan) = p × value(success) + (1 − p) × value(other outcome). Expected gain from changed odds = (p_prepared − p_light) × (value_success − value_other). Probabilities and values come from you; no default effort-to-success coefficient is imposed. Equal odds give no outcome benefit from extra preparation.</p><p><b>Personalized preparation score:</b> 50 + 50 × [w_outcome × (EU_prepared − EU_light)/100 + Σ w_cost × clip((cost_light − cost_prepared)/your_major_change, −1, 1)] / Σw. It uses WAM’s shared preference arithmetic. Above 55 leans toward more preparation; below 45 toward the lighter plan; otherwise close. Hard limits and refusals override it. These cutoffs, cost caps and weights are product conventions, not scientific happiness thresholds. Effort is self-rated overall additional burden from 0–10; time includes recovery.</p><p><b>Break-even odds:</b> p* = p_light − Σ[w_cost × capped cost saving] / [w_outcome × (value_success − value_other)/100]. This is the prepared plan’s success probability needed for score 50, holding everything else fixed. It may exceed 100%, meaning the stated preparation cost cannot break even within this model. The low/high score uses your probability ranges’ opposite corners; it is a sensitivity range, not a statistical confidence interval.</p><p><b>When to stop researching:</b> Information helps when it can change a decision. Expected value of sample information = E_signal[max_action E(utility | signal)] − max_action E(utility). Subtract the personal cost of obtaining it. Perfect information supplies an upper bound; ordinary research is imperfect. This app does not calculate information value without a model of what research might reveal. <a href="https://www2.stat.duke.edu/~scs/Courses/Stat340/LectureSlides/Lec9_ValueInfo_Handouts.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Duke · decision analysis</a>.</p><p><b>Your own evidence:</b> For each plan, the displayed observed success rate is successes / completed attempts. A separately labeled Beta(1,1) estimate is (successes + 1)/(attempts + 2); this prior is an app choice, not evidence. Brier error = mean((forecast probability − observed 0/1 outcome)²); lower is better. Small samples are unstable. Groups match decision type and the exact success definition. Difficulty, selection and other confounders can make preparation correlate with worse or better results; these comparisons do not prove causation or detect a lucky streak. The separately checked preparation model above can supply probabilities when it passes chronological accuracy checks. There is no penalty for being unlucky.</p></details>`;
$('decisionLearning').before(section);
const add=(parent,tag,text)=>{const n=document.createElement(tag);n.textContent=text;parent.append(n);return n;};
for(const [side,title] of [['light','Lighter plan'],['prepared','More prepared plan']]){const f=add($('prepPlans'),'fieldset','');add(f,'legend',title);for(const [key,label,max,step] of [['low','Low plausible success chance · %',100,1],['p','Best estimate of success chance · %',100,1],['high','High plausible success chance · %',100,1],['time','Total planning + recovery time · minutes',100000,1],['money','Total preparation spending · $',1000000,.01],['effort','Overall additional planning burden · 0–10',10,.5]]){const id='prep_'+side+'_'+key,l=add(f,'label',label);l.htmlFor=id;const i=add(f,'input','');i.id=id;i.type='number';i.min=0;i.max=max;i.step=step;i.required=true;}}
for(const [key,label,swing] of [['outcome','Outcome value',null],['time','Planning time',60],['money','Spending',50],['effort','Planning burden',5]]){const f=add($('prepPriorities'),'fieldset','');add(f,'legend',label);const l=add(f,'label','Importance · 0–5');l.htmlFor='prepWeight_'+key;const i=add(f,'input','');i.id=l.htmlFor;i.type='number';i.min=0;i.max=5;i.value=key==='outcome'?5:3;i.required=true;if(swing){for(const [prefix,text,value] of [['Swing','Your major-change amount',swing],['Limit','Optional hard limit for either plan','']]){const l=add(f,'label',text);l.htmlFor='prep'+prefix+'_'+key;const i=add(f,'input','');i.id=l.htmlFor;i.type='number';i.min=prefix==='Swing'?.01:0;i.max=key==='effort'?10:1000000;i.step='.01';i.value=value;i.required=prefix==='Swing';}}}
let snapshot=null;
const num=id=>Number($(id).value);
function input(){const x={success:num('prepSuccess'),failure:num('prepFailure'),weights:{},swings:{},limits:{},declined:$('prepDeclined').checked};for(const s of ['light','prepared']){x[s]={};for(const k of ['low','p','high','time','money','effort'])x[s][k]=num('prep_'+s+'_'+k)/(['low','p','high'].includes(k)?100:1);}for(const k of ['outcome','time','money','effort']){x.weights[k]=num('prepWeight_'+k);if(k!=='outcome'){x.swings[k]=num('prepSwing_'+k);x.limits[k]=$('prepLimit_'+k).value===''?null:num('prepLimit_'+k);}}return x;}
function drawEvidence(){const out=$('prepEvidence');out.replaceChildren();const definition=$('prepDefinition').value.trim();if(!definition){add(out,'p','Define an outcome to see matching observations.');return;}const e=C.evidence(saved,$('prepContext').value,definition),t=add(out,'table',''),head=add(t,'tr','');for(const s of ['Chosen plan','Completed','Observed success','Beta estimate','Mean actual planning time','Brier error'])add(head,'th',s);for(const side of ['light','prepared']){const g=e[side],tr=add(t,'tr','');for(const v of [side,g.n,g.n?(100*g.rate).toFixed(1)+'%':'No data',g.n?(100*g.smoothed).toFixed(1)+'% · prior included':'No data',g.n?g.meanMinutes.toFixed(1)+' min':'—',g.brier!==null?g.brier.toFixed(3):'No probability forecast'])add(tr,'td',String(v));}add(out,'p','Descriptive evidence only. The plans may have been chosen for different difficulties. The separate checked probability model determines whether learned odds can be used.');}
$('prepForm').addEventListener('input',()=>{snapshot=null;$('prepSave').disabled=true;$('prepResult').replaceChildren();$('prepSaveStatus').textContent='Inputs changed. Recalculate before saving.';drawEvidence();});
$('prepForm').onsubmit=e=>{e.preventDefault();const out=$('prepResult');out.replaceChildren();snapshot=null;$('prepSave').disabled=true;try{let x=input();if(root.WamPrepLearning)x=root.WamPrepLearning.resolve(x);const r=C.compare(x);add(out,'h3',r.score.toFixed(1)+'/100 · '+(x.declined?'Respect their answer — step back':r.limits.length?'A hard limit is exceeded':r.preference==='preferred'?'More preparation looks worth it':r.preference==='alternative'?'The lighter plan looks better':'Close call'));add(out,'p','This score favors more preparation above 50. It is a preference comparison, not a happiness forecast or chance of success.');add(out,'p',`Expected outcome value: lighter ${r.expected.light.toFixed(1)}; prepared ${r.expected.prepared.toFixed(1)} /100, before preparation costs. Estimated chance change: ${(r.probabilityChange*100).toFixed(1)} percentage points.`);add(out,'p',`Your probability-range sensitivity: ${r.range.low.toFixed(1)}–${r.range.high.toFixed(1)}/100. `+(r.robust==='uncertain'?'The preferred plan can change across your stated odds.':'The '+(r.robust==='prepared'?'prepared':'lighter')+' plan stays ahead across these stated odds.'));add(out,'p',r.breakEven>1?'Break-even chance exceeds 100%: preparation cannot repay its stated cost in this model.':r.breakEven<0?'The prepared plan breaks even even at 0% success because of its stated resource savings.':`More preparation needs at least ${(r.breakEven*100).toFixed(1)}% success chance to break even with the lighter plan, holding its odds and all costs fixed.`);for(const p of r.parts)add(out,'p',p.label+': '+(p.points>0?'+':'')+p.points.toFixed(1)+' score points'+(p.capped?' · major-change cap reached':''));for(const l of r.limits)add(out,'p',l+'. Revise the plan before acting.');if(x.declined)add(out,'p','Refusal overrides this score. Preparation and spending do not override consent.');snapshot={version:1,context:$('prepContext').value,definition:$('prepDefinition').value.trim(),input:x,result:r,basis:$('prepBasis').value.trim(),ifThen:$('prepIfThen').value.trim()};$('prepSave').disabled=false;$('prepSaveStatus').textContent='Save before the outcome happens to check your forecast later.';drawEvidence();}catch(error){add(out,'p',error.message);const draft=root.WamPrepLearning?.draft(input());if(draft){snapshot=draft;$('prepSave').disabled=false;add(out,'p','No probability-based recommendation yet. Save this forecast without guessed odds, then record the chosen plan and actual outcome to build evidence.');}}};
$('prepExample').onclick=()=>{if($('prepUseLearned')){$('prepUseLearned').checked=false;$('prepUseLearned').dispatchEvent(new Event('change',{bubbles:true}));}const v={prepTask:'Prepare for a class exercise · illustrative example',prepDefinition:'Finish this week’s exercise by Friday',prepSuccess:90,prepFailure:30,prepBasis:'Illustrative guesses only — replace with evidence from comparable classes.',prepIfThen:'If I get stuck for ten minutes, I will ask a question.'};for(const [k,value] of Object.entries(v))$(k).value=value;$('prepContext').value='everyday';$('prepDeclined').checked=false;for(const [side,a] of [['light',[40,50,60,0,0,0]],['prepared',[55,70,80,30,0,2]]])['low','p','high','time','money','effort'].forEach((k,i)=>$('prep_'+side+'_'+k).value=a[i]);for(const k of ['outcome','time','money','effort']){$('prepWeight_'+k).value=k==='outcome'?5:1;if(k!=='outcome'){$('prepLimit_'+k).value='';$('prepSwing_'+k).value={time:60,money:50,effort:5}[k];}}$('prepForm').requestSubmit();};
$('prepSave').onclick=()=>{if(!snapshot)return;const item={id:crypto.randomUUID(),date:new Date().toISOString(),decisionType:'preparation',task:$('prepTask').value.trim(),alt:'Lighter preparation plan',preparationStudy:JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(snapshot)),profileSummary:$('prepResult').textContent+'\nSuccess definition: '+snapshot.definition+'\nEvidence: '+snapshot.basis+'\nIf–then plan: '+snapshot.ifThen,next:''};saved.push(item);if(!persist()){saved.pop();$('prepSaveStatus').textContent='Could not save in this browser.';return;}render();$('prepSave').disabled=true;$('prepSaveStatus').textContent='Forecast saved. Open it in Your reflections after the outcome.';};
function decorate(){const items=saved.slice().reverse();Array.from($('entries').children).forEach((row,i)=>{const item=items[i],s=item?.preparationStudy,details=row.querySelector('details');if(s?.version!==1||!details||details.querySelector('.prep-followup'))return;const f=add(details,'fieldset','');f.className='prep-followup';add(f,'legend','Preparation outcome');add(f,'p','Success means: '+s.definition);const choice=add(f,'select','');choice.setAttribute('aria-label','Preparation plan chosen for '+item.task);for(const [value,label] of [['','Choose the plan you actually used…'],['light',item.decisionType==='preparation'?'Lighter plan':item.alt],['prepared',item.decisionType==='preparation'?'More prepared plan':item.task]])choice.add(new Option(label,value));choice.value=s.chosen||'';const minutes=add(f,'input','');minutes.type='number';minutes.min=0;minutes.max=100000;minutes.step='1';minutes.placeholder='Actual planning + recovery minutes';minutes.setAttribute('aria-label','Actual preparation minutes for '+item.task);minutes.value=s.actual?.minutes??'';const outcome=add(f,'select','');outcome.setAttribute('aria-label','Defined preparation outcome for '+item.task);for(const [v,l] of [['','Select after the deadline…'],['yes','Success happened'],['no','Other outcome happened']])outcome.add(new Option(l,v));outcome.value=s.actual?String(s.actual.success?'yes':'no'):'';const check=add(f,'input','');check.type='checkbox';check.style.width='auto';check.setAttribute('aria-label','Confirm preparation outcome for '+item.task);add(f,'span',' The deadline has passed and these describe the plan I actually used.');const button=add(f,'button','Save preparation outcome');button.type='button';button.className='quiet';const status=add(f,'p','');status.setAttribute('role','status');choice.onchange=()=>{minutes.value='';outcome.value='';check.checked=false;};button.onclick=()=>{if(!choice.value||!outcome.value||minutes.value===''||!minutes.checkValidity()||!check.checked){status.textContent='Choose the actual plan, valid minutes and outcome, then confirm after the deadline.';return;}const before=JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(s)),oldChoice=item.outcomeChoice,oldActual=item.actualChoice;s.chosen=choice.value;if(item.decisionType!=='preparation'){item.outcomeChoice=choice.value==='prepared'?'do':'alt';item.actualChoice=item.outcomeChoice;}s.actual={minutes:Number(minutes.value),success:outcome.value==='yes',recordedAt:new Date().toISOString()};if(!persist()){for(const key of Object.keys(s))delete s[key];Object.assign(s,before);item.outcomeChoice=oldChoice;item.actualChoice=oldActual;status.textContent='Could not save.';return;}status.textContent='Outcome saved. This checks your forecast; it does not measure luck or prove a causal effect.';drawEvidence();document.dispatchEvent(new Event('wam:preparation-updated'));};});drawEvidence();}
const oldRender=render;render=function(){oldRender();decorate();};document.addEventListener('wam:history-restored',decorate);decorate();
})(typeof globalThis!=='undefined'?globalThis:this);
